<ul data-start="461" data-end="819">
<li data-start="461" data-end="585">
<p data-start="463" data-end="585"><strong data-start="463" data-end="488">Φ (scalar potential):</strong> Represents <strong data-start="500" data-end="542">latent creative and economic potential</strong> distributed across agents and communities.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="586" data-end="695">
<p data-start="588" data-end="695"><strong data-start="588" data-end="610">𝒗 (vector field):</strong> Represents <strong data-start="622" data-end="694">directional flows of capital, attention, and informational influence</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="696" data-end="819">
<p data-start="698" data-end="819"><strong data-start="698" data-end="722">S (entropy density):</strong> Represents the <strong data-start="738" data-end="774">degree of disorder or inequality</strong> in the system, constrained by RSVP dynamics.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="821" data-end="969">The manifold <strong data-start="834" data-end="839">ℳ</strong> corresponds to <strong data-start="855" data-end="885">social-informational space</strong> where agents, institutions, and infrastructures are nodes in a continuous topology.</p>
<hr data-start="971" data-end="974">
<h3 data-start="976" data-end="1006"><strong data-start="980" data-end="1006">II. Governing Dynamics</strong></h3>
<p data-start="1007" data-end="1085">RSVP assumes a <strong data-start="1022" data-end="1044">Lagrangian density</strong> capturing energy and entropy trade-offs:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">L</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mo>⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="script">v</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L} = \frac{1}{2} (\nabla \Phi)^2 + \alpha \, \Phi \, \nabla \cdot \mathcal{v} - \beta S \log S - \gamma \Phi S</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal">L</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 2.0074em; vertical-align: -0.686em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mopen nulldelimiter"></span><span class="mfrac"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.3214em;"><span style="top: -2.314em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">2</span></span></span><span style="top: -3.23em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="frac-line" style="border-bottom-width: 0.04em;"></span></span><span style="top: -3.677em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.686em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose nulldelimiter"></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">∇Φ</span><span class="mclose"><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8641em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0037em;">α</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">∇</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6667em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">βS</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mop">lo<span style="margin-right: 0.01389em;">g</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8778em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05556em;">γ</span><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="1214" data-end="1220">where:</p>
<ul data-start="1221" data-end="1647">
<li data-start="1221" data-end="1338">
<p data-start="1223" data-end="1338"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\nabla \Phi)^2</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.0641em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">∇Φ</span><span class="mclose"><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8141em;"><span style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> captures <strong data-start="1252" data-end="1271">gradient energy</strong> in scalar potential (how evenly creative capacity is distributed).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1339" data-end="1448">
<p data-start="1341" data-end="1448"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mo>⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="script">v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha \Phi \nabla \cdot \mathcal{v}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0037em;">α</span><span class="mord">Φ∇</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span></span></span></span> represents <strong data-start="1393" data-end="1447">alignment of capital flows with creative potential</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1449" data-end="1531">
<p data-start="1451" data-end="1531"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\beta S \log S</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord">−</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">βS</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mop">lo<span style="margin-right: 0.01389em;">g</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span></span></span></span> models <strong data-start="1478" data-end="1500">entropic smoothing</strong>: high entropy seeks diffusion.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1532" data-end="1647">
<p data-start="1534" data-end="1647"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\gamma \Phi S</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8778em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord">−</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05556em;">γ</span><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span></span></span></span> penalizes regions where <strong data-start="1577" data-end="1621">high potential and high entropy coincide</strong> (structural instability).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1649" data-end="1660">The action:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">S</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi mathvariant="script">M</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="script">L</mi><mtext> </mtext><msup><mi>d</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S} = \int_{\mathcal{M}} \mathcal{L} \, d^n x</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.075em;">S</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 2.2719em; vertical-align: -0.9119em;"></span><span class="mop"><span class="mop op-symbol large-op" style="margin-right: 0.44445em; position: relative; top: -0.0011em;">∫</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist"><span style="top: -1.7881em; margin-left: -0.4445em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathcal mtight">M</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.9119em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal">L</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">d</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.7144em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">n</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="1723" data-end="1754">and equilibrium states satisfy:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mi mathvariant="script">S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta \mathcal{S} = 0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03785em;">δ</span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.075em;">S</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="1786" data-end="1850">subject to <strong data-start="1797" data-end="1849">boundary conditions imposed by global capitalism</strong>.</p>
<hr data-start="1852" data-end="1855">
<h3 data-start="1857" data-end="1921"><strong data-start="1861" data-end="1921">III. Attractor Formation in Hollywood and Silicon Valley</strong></h3>
<p data-start="1922" data-end="2115">Empirically, these systems exhibit <strong data-start="1957" data-end="1981">localized attractors</strong>—nodes with extreme <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">Φ</span></span></span></span> concentration (celebrity, unicorn founders) and strong <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{v}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span></span></span></span> convergence (capital + attention).</p>
<p data-start="2117" data-end="2161">We define <strong data-start="2127" data-end="2157">localized coherence states</strong> as:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>∼</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo separator="true">,</mo><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mo>⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="script">v</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mtext>&nbsp;near&nbsp;</mtext><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(x) \sim \delta(x - x_0), \quad \nabla \cdot \mathcal{v} &lt; 0 \text{ near } x_0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∼</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03785em;">δ</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">0</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">∇</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.5782em; vertical-align: -0.0391em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">&lt;</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7944em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">&nbsp;near&nbsp;</span></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">0</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="2253" data-end="2522">where <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.5806em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">0</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> is a node representing <strong data-start="2290" data-end="2326">a founder, star, or iconic brand</strong>.<br data-start="2327" data-end="2330">
This corresponds to a <strong data-start="2352" data-end="2372">phase transition</strong> in the RSVP plenum: a globally diffuse Φ field collapses into one or few attractors, increasing <strong data-start="2469" data-end="2486">order locally</strong> while raising global entropy <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span></span></span></span>.</p>
<hr data-start="2524" data-end="2527">
<h3 data-start="2529" data-end="2578"><strong data-start="2533" data-end="2578">IV. Entropy Dynamics and Myth Maintenance</strong></h3>
<p data-start="2579" data-end="2610">The RSVP entropy flux equation:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">∂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>S</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mo>⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="script">v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi mathvariant="script">v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_t S + \nabla \cdot (S \mathcal{v}) = \sigma(\Phi, \mathcal{v})</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8444em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord" style="margin-right: 0.05556em;">∂</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0556em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">∇</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">σ</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="2691" data-end="2875">where <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi mathvariant="script">v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(\Phi, \mathcal{v})</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">σ</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> is an <strong data-start="2733" data-end="2760">entropy production term</strong> linked to <strong data-start="2771" data-end="2796">narrative myth-making</strong>. Myths stabilize high-coherence attractors by reducing <strong data-start="2852" data-end="2874">perceived disorder</strong>:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>κ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>ˉ</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma = \lambda (\Phi^\kappa - \bar{\Phi})</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">σ</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">λ</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.7144em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">κ</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.0701em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord accent"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8201em;"><span style="top: -3em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord">Φ</span></span><span style="top: -3.2523em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="accent-body" style="left: -0.25em;"><span class="mord">ˉ</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="2928" data-end="3064">where <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">λ</span></span></span></span> and <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">κ</span></span></span></span> are <strong data-start="2965" data-end="3008">parameters of ideological amplification</strong> (Hollywood storytelling, Silicon Valley founder myths).</p>
<hr data-start="3066" data-end="3069">
<h3 data-start="3071" data-end="3124"><strong data-start="3075" data-end="3124">V. Community Fragility as a Field Instability</strong></h3>
<p data-start="3125" data-end="3292">Household stability corresponds to <strong data-start="3160" data-end="3199">distributed Φ across multiple nodes</strong> with low entropy coupling.<br data-start="3226" data-end="3229">
The myth of the <strong data-start="3245" data-end="3282">single breadwinner or lone genius</strong> enforces:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≫</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">∀</mi><mi>j</mi><mo mathvariant="normal">≠</mo><mi>i</mi><mtext>&nbsp;in&nbsp;local&nbsp;cluster</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_i \gg \Phi_j \, \forall j \neq i \text{ in local cluster}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">i</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">≫</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.9805em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.05724em;">j</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">∀</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05724em;">j</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel"><span class="mrel"><span class="mord vbox"><span class="thinbox"><span class="rlap"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="inner"><span class="mord"><span class="mrel"></span></span></span><span class="fix"></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mrel">=</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">i</span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">&nbsp;in&nbsp;local&nbsp;cluster</span></span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="3364" data-end="3503">creating <strong data-start="3373" data-end="3398">structural anisotropy</strong>. In RSVP terms, this reduces redundancy and increases <strong data-start="3453" data-end="3502">susceptibility to collapse under perturbation</strong>.</p>
<hr data-start="3505" data-end="3508">
<h3 data-start="3510" data-end="3553"><strong data-start="3514" data-end="3553">VI. Alternative RSVP Configurations</strong></h3>
<p data-start="3554" data-end="3643">To counteract <strong data-start="3568" data-end="3594">singularity attractors</strong>, RSVP suggests <strong data-start="3610" data-end="3642">distributed coherence states</strong>:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>≈</mo><mtext>constant</mtext><mo separator="true">,</mo><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mo>⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="script">v</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(x) \approx \text{constant}, \quad \nabla \cdot \mathcal{v} \approx 0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">≈</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8778em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">constant</span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">∇</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4831em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">≈</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="3726" data-end="3739">achieved via:</p>
<ul data-start="3740" data-end="3973">
<li data-start="3740" data-end="3816">
<p data-start="3742" data-end="3816"><strong data-start="3742" data-end="3762">Vector diffusion</strong>: spreading capital flows across cooperative clusters.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3817" data-end="3901">
<p data-start="3819" data-end="3901"><strong data-start="3819" data-end="3847">Entropy-aware regulation</strong>: imposing constraints on <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∣</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∣</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Phi(x)|</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">∣Φ</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mord">∣</span></span></span></span> concentration.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3902" data-end="3973">
<p data-start="3904" data-end="3973"><strong data-start="3904" data-end="3938">Multi-scale attractor networks</strong>: preventing unilateral phase-lock.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="3975" data-end="3978">
<h3 data-start="3980" data-end="4007"><strong data-start="3984" data-end="4007">VII. Interpretation</strong></h3>
<p data-start="4008" data-end="4332">Under RSVP, Hollywood and Silicon Valley are <strong data-start="4053" data-end="4076">not moral anomalies</strong> but <strong data-start="4081" data-end="4169">necessary outcomes of boundary conditions that minimize local entropy at global cost</strong>.<br data-start="4170" data-end="4173">
Their persistence follows from the <strong data-start="4208" data-end="4233">variational principle</strong>: the system seeks <strong data-start="4252" data-end="4272">coherence minima</strong>, which under current rules favor <strong data-start="4306" data-end="4331">extreme individualism</strong>.</p>
<hr data-start="4334" data-end="4337">
